<%# Income Tax result (spec issue #260, DESIGN.md §4) — the iteration's bracket-math
    primitive rendered. It composes BLEND components:
      • Hero-result — the total federal income tax (5px coral left rule, big tabular-nums),
        the cost figure, with the taxable income it was computed on read into the sentence.
      • Stat grid   — taxable income, after-tax income, effective rate, marginal rate. The
        money figures can run to 7+ digits ($216,020.25 on a $700k income) and a worst case
        ($1,000,000+ income → 6-figure tax) so the grid takes the `--wide` track (DESIGN.md
        §4: high-magnitude money → --wide so values hold on one line, never wrap mid-number).
        After-tax income (what you keep) reads in accent green (DESIGN.md §1 — the positive
        figure).
      • Data table  — the per-bracket breakdown (the `tabular-output`): each bracket's range,
        rate, the amount taxed in it, and the tax — thin rule borders, right-aligned
        tabular-nums, a hard ink total row whose tax reconciles to total_tax (DESIGN.md §4
        "Data table"). No chart for this build (spec: the table suffices).
    The backend owns every number (ARCHITECTURE.md §4); this only renders the envelope —
    money/rate strings and the bracket rows. `calc:` is a valid Calculators::IncomeTax. %>
<% r = calc.result %>
<% brackets = income_tax_brackets(calc) %>
<div class="space-y-6">
  <%# ── Hero: the total tax ──────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
      <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Total federal income tax</p>
        <p class="mt-2 flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-sm font-bold text-faint">$</span>
          <span class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= money_display(r[:total_tax]) %></span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          on <span class="font-semibold text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:taxable_income]) %></span>
          of taxable income — an effective rate of
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= percentage_display(BigDecimal(r[:effective_rate])) %>%</span>,
          with your top dollar taxed at <span class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= r[:marginal_rate] %>%</span>
          (2025 single-filer brackets).
        </p>

        <%# Breakdown — the shared responsive stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", issue #143):
            `.stat-grid` / `.stat-card`. The `--wide` modifier widens the auto-fit track (13rem)
            so a high-magnitude money figure (after-tax income on a $700k income → $483,979.75,
            and the worst case past $1M) holds on one line rather than wrapping at the cents
            (DESIGN.md §4: stats must never clip/wrap). After-tax income is the positive/kept
            figure → accent green (DESIGN.md §1); the rest read in ink. %>
        <dl class="mt-6 stat-grid stat-grid--wide">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Taxable income</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words">$<%= money_display(r[:taxable_income]) %></dd>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">After-tax income</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-accent break-words">$<%= money_display(r[:after_tax_income]) %></dd>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Effective rate</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words"><%= percentage_display(BigDecimal(r[:effective_rate])) %>%</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Marginal rate</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words"><%= r[:marginal_rate] %>%</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Per-bracket breakdown (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table") ─────────────────────
      The `tabular-output`: one row per bracket the income reaches (rows below the marginal
      bracket are full, the marginal row is partial). Thin rule borders, right-aligned
      tabular-nums, a hard ink total row whose tax reconciles to total_tax. When taxable income
      is 0 no bracket is reached → the brackets array is empty; show a quiet "no tax" note
      instead of an empty table. %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="px-6 pt-6">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">How your tax is built — bracket by bracket</p>
    </div>

    <% if brackets.empty? %>
      <p class="px-6 py-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        No taxable income reaches a bracket, so no federal income tax is owed.
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule text-left text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-faint">
              <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 font-bold">Bracket</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right font-bold">Rate</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right font-bold">Taxed in bracket</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right font-bold">Tax</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% brackets.each do |row| %>
              <tr class="border-b border-rule/70 text-ink last:border-0">
                <%# The bracket's taxed range — the raw bracket edges echoed back to the user,
                    so per DESIGN.md §2 they render in monospace <code> (font-mono). %>
                <td class="px-6 py-2.5 text-muted">
                  <code class="font-mono text-[13px] tabular-nums"><%= income_tax_bracket_range(row) %></code>
                </td>
                <td class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right tabular-nums"><%= row[:rate] %>%</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(row[:taxable_in_bracket]) %></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right tabular-nums font-semibold">$<%= money_display(row[:tax]) %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
          <tfoot>
            <%# Hard total row — top border in ink (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table"). The tax column
                sums to total_tax (Σ brackets[*].tax == total_tax, per the spec). %>
            <tr class="border-t-2 border-ink bg-bg/40 font-bold text-ink">
              <td class="px-6 py-3">Total</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-3"></td>
              <td class="px-6 py-3 text-right tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(r[:taxable_income]) %></td>
              <td class="px-6 py-3 text-right tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(r[:total_tax]) %></td>
            </tr>
          </tfoot>
        </table>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
